here's a really important political  story that crosses the the virus story  it crosses 2020 election it crosses the  Democratic primary storyline separation  of powers really a lot of stories are  involved here Democratic Speaker of the  House Nancy Pelosi is now calling for  the country to vote by mail period now  of course with coronavirus raging and  ravaging the country as we now get into  the phase of the pandemic where the  daily death toll is staggering there are  more and more questions about what's the  rest of the Democratic primary going to  look like but also what's the November  election going to look like a bunch of  Democratic primaries have already been  postponed because of the virus some  states have already decided they are  going to vote by mail or rather some  states already vote by mail others are  trying to figure out what can they do to  get going in that direction but  eventually we're going to get to the  November general election  now I've received dozens and dozens of  emails from people saying is Trump going  to try to postpone the election in  November is Trump going to try to use  the virus to stay in office indefinitely  will it be safe to go out and vote in  November won't the trumpets who don't  take the virus seriously go out and vote  whereas Democrats who are more likely to  take the virus seriously it will stay  home helping Donald Trump getting  helping Donald Trump to get reelected  well of course the answer is we should  be able to vote by mail and Nancy Pelosi  is now saying that's exactly what should  happen which is going to become one of  the biggest political fights since  impeachment here is Nancy Pelosi saying  it on MSNBC yesterday in terms of the  elections I think that will probably be  moving to vote-by-mail that's why we  want it to have more resources in this  third bill that just was signed by the  president to get those resources to the  states to facilitate the reality of life  that we are going to have to have more  vote-by-mail and would hope that we  would have also some funding which was  rejected for the postal service which is  what implement the vote by mail as well  as implementing right now getting  equipment to where it needs to be so  that's very clear she says we need to  vote by mail  the problem is Republicans don't  this Trump doesn't want this Trump  actually said this week vote-by-mail is  one of the package of ideas that  Democrats wanted in the stimulus bill  that would hurt Republicans I won't tell  you this if you look at before and after  the things they had in there were crazy  they had things levels of voting that if  they ever agreed to it you'd never have  a Republican elected in this country  again they had things in there about you  know election days and what you do and  all sorts of clawbacks  and they had things that were just  totally crazy and had nothing to do with  workers that lost their jobs one of  those crazy things that Democrats wanted  in the bill that would make it so  Republicans don't win is people voting  by mail they had things levels of voting  that if you agreed to it Republicans  wouldn't win ever again said Donald  Trump so they know that when more people  vote it's not good for Republicans so  let's talk about how this applies to the  November election we know Democrats are  taking stay-at-home Orders more  seriously than Republicans we know  Democrats are taking the coronavirus  more seriously than Republicans if that  continues if the pandemic persists and  you have to vote in person more  Democrats are going to stay home and  that will allow trumpets to likely get  Donald Trump re-elected because they are  more likely to be ignoring stay-at-home  orders if they even have them in their  states so this is going to be a major  fight it's good that Nancy Pelosi is  bringing this up this should not be  controversial we've had absentee ballots  for years absentee ballots are a form of  vote by mail some people are able to do  it because they can justify it they're  either going to be away unable to vote  in person for whatever other reason  we're talking just about expanding  absentee voting to everyone we have the  system they are going to argue  Republicans that it's too short notice  we simply can't do it we have the  systems in place states already have  vote-by-mail in the sense of absentee  ballots we're simply saying allow  everyone to get an absentee ballot this  is another reason why Trump wants to  open things back up if  things are open it's harder to justify  vote-by-mail if things remain closed  because of the pandemic if states are  still under stay-at-home orders or sort  of shutdown guidelines it is more likely  that Nancy Pelosi would be able to get  her way  on vote-by-mail would be actually a  fantastic modernization of our election  system to switch to 100% vote by mail  people don't need to go stand in line  all bunched together spending sometimes  hours in line voting vote by mail it  makes sense Trump and Republicans know  it's an existential threat for Trump  second term so they will do everything  they can to prevent it but we should do  it we'll continue to cover this and  other stories from today's show on the  David Pakman show  instagram page at david pakman show  while you're on instagram make sure  you're following me for the latest  coronavirus boredom updates on my  Instagram page David Pakman
 

